WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:24.531
"Today we're going to turn our old crayons into rainbow candles," Miss Shelly said.

2
00:00:24.532 --> 00:00:27.727
She held up a colorful, striped candle.

3
00:00:27.728 --> 00:00:31.544
Nina looked into her bag of old, broken crayons.

4
00:00:31.545 --> 00:00:36.284
She wasn't sure she wanted her purple crayons in a rainbow candle.

5
00:00:36.285 --> 00:00:40.428
"First let's see what colors we have," said Miss Shelly.

6
00:00:40.429 --> 00:00:43.952
The kids emptied their bags of crayons onto the table.

7
00:00:43.953 --> 00:00:54.495
"We've got red, orange, yellow, blue, green, and . . . lots of purple from Nina!" Miss Shelly said.

8
00:00:54.496 --> 00:00:57.453
"Perfect for rainbow candles."

9
00:00:57.454 --> 00:00:59.889
Nina raised her hand.

10
00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.541
"Miss Shelly, can I make a purple candle?

11
00:01:03.542 --> 00:01:06.103
I don't want a rainbow candle."

12
00:01:06.104 --> 00:01:07.679
Miss Shelly paused.

13
00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:11.473
"Well, we're all going to share crayons.

14
00:01:11.474 --> 00:01:14.997
If you only want purple, it may be a short candle.

15
00:01:14.998 --> 00:01:17.026
Is that okay?"

16
00:01:17.027 --> 00:01:22.131
Nina nodded. "Uh-huh. As long as it's purple."

17
00:01:22.132 --> 00:01:29.484
"Okay. First we need to peel the paper off the crayons," Miss Shelly said.

18
00:01:29.485 --> 00:01:32.825
"We don't want the paper in our candles."

19
00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:37.792
When the kids were done, Miss Shelly lit the hot plate.

20
00:01:37.793 --> 00:01:41.387
"Now we'll melt the crayons, one color at a time.

21
00:01:41.388 --> 00:01:45.531
We'll melt them in this top pot," she said.

22
00:01:45.532 --> 00:01:48.463
"Red crayons please."

23
00:01:48.464 --> 00:01:54.868
The kids dropped handfuls of red crayons into the pot.

24
00:01:54.869 --> 00:01:58.667
"Ooh, they're melting!" Jason said.

25
00:01:58.668 --> 00:02:04.242
"Be careful. The pot is very hot!" Miss Shelly warned.

26
00:02:04.243 --> 00:02:08.356
"Now we pour the wax into your glass jars.

27
00:02:08.357 --> 00:02:12.126
Carefully hold the wick in the center of your jar like this.

28
00:02:12.127 --> 00:02:13.954
I'll pour the wax.

29
00:02:13.955 --> 00:02:18.039
Do not let go of your wick!" Miss Shelly said.

30
00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:24.685
She poured a layer of red wax into the bottom of Izzie's jar, Jason's jar, and then Bobby's jar.

31
00:02:24.686 --> 00:02:31.094
She did the same for orange, yellow, green, and blue wax.

32
00:02:31.095 --> 00:02:33.110
Nina just watched.

33
00:02:33.111 --> 00:02:35.596
Her jar was empty.

34
00:02:35.597 --> 00:02:40.297
"Here we go. The last layer," Miss Shelly said.

35
00:02:40.298 --> 00:02:43.302
Nina jumped up and held out her jar.

36
00:02:43.303 --> 00:02:47.125
Finally they were ready for purple!

37
00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:53.395
Miss Shelly poured everyone some purple wax.

38
00:02:53.396 --> 00:02:59.812
"Miss Shelly, my candle doesn't reach the top of my jar," Nina said, frowning.

39
00:02:59.813 --> 00:03:03.685
"Nina, I warned you about that," Miss Shelly said.

40
00:03:03.686 --> 00:03:09.622
"I know. But I didn't think it was going to look like this!" Nina said.

41
00:03:09.623 --> 00:03:14.328
She looked sadly at her short candle with its long, droopy wick.

42
00:03:14.329 --> 00:03:18.760
"I've still got some red crayons," Bobby said.

43
00:03:18.761 --> 00:03:21.475
"And Jason has blue crayons.

44
00:03:21.476 --> 00:03:23.894
Red and blue make purple.

45
00:03:23.895 --> 00:03:26.577
We can make more purple wax."

46
00:03:26.578 --> 00:03:29.575
Bobby looked at Miss Shelly.

47
00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:31.323
Nina smiled at Bobby.

48
00:03:31.324 --> 00:03:33.472
"Thanks," she said.

49
00:03:33.473 --> 00:03:36.487
Sometimes he was nice.

50
00:03:36.488 --> 00:03:47.827
They melted the red and blue crayons together in the pot.

51
00:03:47.828 --> 00:03:49.785
"I think that will do.

52
00:03:49.786 --> 00:03:53.320
Don't you?" Miss Shelly asked Nina.

53
00:03:53.321 --> 00:03:56.854
Nina's candle wasn't as tall as the rainbow candles.

54
00:03:56.855 --> 00:04:00.592
But now it almost reached the top of her jar.

55
00:04:00.593 --> 00:04:06.374
"Yeah. It's better," she said.

56
00:04:06.375 --> 00:04:09.700
Later Miss Shelly trimmed everyone's wicks.

57
00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:14.177
Then she lit the candles and turned off the lights.

58
00:04:14.178 --> 00:04:17.600
Everyone's candles flickered brightly in the dark.

59
00:04:17.601 --> 00:04:22.046
"Our candles look awesome!" Jason said.

60
00:04:22.047 --> 00:04:26.465
"Your rainbow candle is really pretty," Nina told Izzie.

61
00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:30.636
"Thanks. Your purple one is too," Izzie said.

62
00:04:30.637 --> 00:04:35.869
Nina looked at her Kids Central friends and teacher in the glowing lights.

63
00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:43.343
She couldn't imagine school without them!
